+- Removing a user from an organization (`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}`, for offboarding):
+  - The organization must be the caller's, else 404. The user must belong to it, else 404.
+  - Only org admins may do it; anyone else in the organization gets 403.
+  - The user's memberships in all of the organization's projects are removed, and tasks they
+    were assigned in those projects become unassigned (an assignee must be a member).
+  - The user's org-admin role is cleared, so they can no longer read the organization's projects.
+    The user row is kept.
+  - This is allowed in archived projects too, so archiving never blocks offboarding (exception
+    to the archived rule above).
+  - Repeating the request answers 204 again and changes nothing.
 
